n" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2b0550090cc26f93266a7b0f166dd854d1a1cbe6f6ecc0508c6c1b68bfd5def3" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" "basis" 1386 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039806/state.json" "file_sha256" "c67ab59a49029f9e2c4f22a62a9d91369e26fc6ab6019728ac68fd5c32866ba8" 