"⟨15,5,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,5,12⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19779" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-15,3,5⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=⟨\\frac{2}{3},0,1⟩$ and $v=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$\n\n$u\\times v=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((0)(-3)-(1)(2))i-((\\frac{2}{3})(-3)-(1)(1))j+((\\frac{2}{3})(2)-(0)(1))k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(-2-1)j+(\\frac{4}{3})k \\\\  & =-2i+3j+(\\frac{4}{3})k \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,\\frac{4}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-281977" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨2x,5,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{393}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 2x & 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 2x & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2x & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4-15)i-(2x-6x)j+(5x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨-11,4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+121} & =\\sqrt{393} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+121 & =393 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =272 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-5"] ["math" "x=-5,-4"] ["math" "x=4,5"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"] ["math" "x=\\pm 5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-19785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,0,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,2,0⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{29}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 0 & 1 \\\\ -x & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-2)i-(0+x)j+(2x+0)k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-x,2x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+4} & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4 & =29 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\sqrt{5},$ $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282261" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-282278" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-77427" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-278839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨x,2,1⟩,$ $b=⟨2,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{20}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-278839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(x-2)j+(0-4)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-x,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-x)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4-4x+{x}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-4x+24} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+24 & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-278839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "41fc45be10d253903f4a5ba30969c2f07263528c23e0fe7e1b3b153fe814c217"} {"question" "q-278839" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "q-278839" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/state.json" "file_sha256" "b825a880e0e1d736e658c43725177f229e73a63bea6543a4de20979979f69828"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "d6ef00ca3496dfae50ebfb26f7f574eff0cc999a3ba4bec8f379d09de459aa16"} {"question" "e-4341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/example-4341.json" "file_sha256" "d6ef00ca3496dfae50ebfb26f7f574eff0cc999a3ba4bec8f379d09de459aa16"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "8b45fc78ccc1197c71f0d4da04be969949fb0b88e3803673fb7b473dacd30718"} {"question" "e-4343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076277/example-4343.json" "file_sha256" "8b45fc78ccc1197c71f0d4da04be969949fb0b88e3803673fb7b473dacd30718"} {"question" "q-1405" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-18,19,-61⟩"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questi